[pgndiagram] And black has reasonable play here.}) 15. Rfd1 Rac8 (15... e5 {
[pgndiagram] Is not so effective.} 16. Nb5 e4 17. Bc2 Nd5 18. Qg4 {And now
there is no f5, since Black has moved the rook away. This is what it means "to
get a game". These complex positions are very hard to understand.}) 16. Rac1 (
16. Nb5 $5 {[pgndiagram] Commentators on chessgames, and my engine like this
move. White is consistent in his plan and puts his knight on b5} Nf8 {Now this
maneovre is met strongly} 17. b4 $1 {The point} axb4 18. axb4 Bxb4 19. Nxb6 Rc6
20. Nc4 {[pgndiagram] And despite the symmetry, Black's pieces are somewhat
