[pgndiagram] Again being agressive, which doesn't spoil anything yet, though.}
Ned7 29. Na7 Qa3 $1 {This is a great move, and was allowed by White's 28th
move.} 30. Nc6 (30. Rxd7 {[pgndiagram]} Nxd7 31. Qxd7 Qxe3+ 32. Kf1 Qc1+ {
[pgndiagram] And Black has at least perpetual}) 30... Rf8 31. h3 {[pgndiagram]
Getting some "luft", and threatening Rxd7.} Nc5 {Now the a4 is a "gooner".
White has to demonstrate that he has sufficient play for it. Another important
point is that both players had around 6 minutes on the clock at this point.}
32. Kh2 Nxa4 33. Rd8 $6 (33. e4 {[pgndiagram], Was a possibility.} Nc5 34. e5
Nh5 35. Qf2 g6 36. g4 Ng7 37. Qh4 {Apparently White has enough play here.} Qe3
{[pgndiagram]} (37... Kh7 $6 {[pgndiagram] Would lose the f7 pawn, which I
