square for the White knight.}) 10. axb5 axb5 11. Na3 O-O 12. Nxb5 {[pgndiagram]
The typical position for this variation is on the board. White has captured
the b-pawn, but he is behind in development.} Bg4 {Exerting pressure to the
centre.} (12... Nxe4 $4 {Is never advisable in this variation.} 13. Bd5) 13.
Bc2 (13. d5 {[pgndiagram]Trying to save the pawn without concesion is second
