Only not this move} Raf8 30. Re3 d4 31. cxd4 exd4 32. Nxd4 Rxf2+ {[pgndiagram]
And Black is winning probably}) 29... Kd6 30. Nf3 Raf8 31. Ng5 Re7 {
[pgndiagram] Black can only wait passively and see from which way will White's
punches come} 32. Rae1 {White is probing the e-pawn} Rfe8 {And Black defends}
33. Nf3 Nh8 $6 {Knight is heading f7 and then f5 potentially, but this should
be too slow} (33... Nf8 $5 {[pgndiagram] Is interesting, but to Black still
has problems} 34. b4 $1 {Emphasizing that Black has weaknesses both in the
centre and on the queenside} Nd7 35. bxa5 Ra8 {The critical moment} (35... Nc5
{[pgndiagram] Would run into tactical blow} 36. Nxe5 Kxe5 37. d4+) 36. d4 $1 {
[pgndiagram] Now when the Black has removed the rook, striking in the centre.
