maneouvre in the future} (36. b4 {Was possible an almost every White move} axb4
37. cxb4 e5 38. Nb3 d4 39. f4 Nf7 {[pgndiagram] But here White ends up in an
inferior version of the endgame. e5-d4 probably shouldn't be allowed}) 36...
Nf7 (36... e5 37. Nb3 b6 38. Rd1 {[pgndiagram] The king in the centre is a
problem} Ke6 39. exd5+ cxd5 40. Nc1 Nf7 41. Ne2 {[pgndiagram] And Nf4 threat
