1. e4 {Saric has played only 1 e4 his entire life} c6 {While 1...c6 is
Zelcic's main response} 2. d4 d5 3. e5 {I think this is the most critical
continuation - sometimes Saric never shies away from} Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 5. Be2 {
Nigel Short is the one responsible for the popularity of this quiet system in
the advance variation} c5 {This is a natural move, but also a dangerous one -
in some variations Black runs into problems on the queenside} 6. Be3 (6. c3 {
Gives Black a good version of the French defence}) 6... Qb6 (6... cxd4 7. Nxd4
{Is bad for Black}) 7. Nc3 $1 {The point!} Nc6 (7... Qxb2 {Can be met by either
} 8. Nb5 ({Or the surprising} 8. Qb1 $5 Qxb1+ (8... Qxc3+ {Loses to} 9. Bd2) 9.
Rxb1 {And now Black's best is to play} c4 (9... b6 10. dxc5 bxc5 11. Rb7 {Is
considered as better for White}))) 8. O-O Qxb2 9. Qe1 {This is all theory,
obviously} (9. Qb1 {Is now bad. After} Qxb1 10. Rfxb1 {Black can go} O-O-O {
And he is fine}) (9. Nb5 {Has also been played} c4 10. Nc7+ Kd7 11. Nxa8 Bxc2 {
And it is not clear who is better}) 9... cxd4 10. Bxd4 Nxd4 11. Nxd4 Bb4 12.
Rb1 Qxc3 13. Rxb4 Qxe1 (13... Qc7 {Is too risky. White has several good
continuations. The best might be immediate strike with} 14. c4 (14. Nb5 Qxe5 {
Is not so clear})) 14. Rxe1 {The smoke has cleared. White has sacrificed a
pawn, but he has a lead in development and Black has trouble on the queenside,
which gives him sufficient compensation} b6 {Black can't allow Rxb7} 15. h4 {
But this is not the first move that comes to mind. I am not 100% sure, but
there is high probability Saric was still within his preparation} (15. Nxf5
exf5 16. Bb5+ {Is also possible, but the inclusion of h4 and h5 is in White's
favour (opens the route for the king and creates a potential target on g6)}) (
15. Nb5) (15. Bb5+) 15... h5 {But this is a mistake, creating too many
weaknesses} (15... Be4 {Is the comp's suggestion} 16. f3 Bg6 {And now h5 is
not possible} 17. Bb5+ Kf8 18. Re3 {And White has definite compensation. But
not more}) (15... Bg6 {Loses on the spot} 16. h5) 16. Nxf5 exf5 17. Bb5+ Kf8 (
17... Ke7 {I didn't understand what is wrong with this move} 18. Rd4 Ke6 19. c4
{But then the engine quickly made me realize this typical move leads to
decisive advantage}) 18. Rd1 Ne7 19. c4 {Remember this shot, dear readers.
Undermining the center with c4 happens often in these advance Caro positions}
d4 {Trying to keep the position closed} (19... dxc4 20. Rxc4 {And White's rook
are tremendously active. Black can't even go} Rc8 21. Rxc8+ Nxc8 22. Rd8+) 20.
Rxd4 Rh6 21. Ra4 {But now Black has a very unpleasant endgame} Nc6 22. Rd5 Re6
23. f4 g6 24. c5 {White  could have also considered Rd7. It is probably better
than what happened in the game} (24. Rd7 Na5 25. c5 Re7 26. cxb6 axb6 27. Rd6 {
But I agree it is not so easy to evaluate this for a human.}) 24... bxc5 25.
Rxc5 Nd8 26. Bc4 Re7 27. Bd5 Rb8 28. Rca5 Rb1+ 29. Kf2 Rd7 30. Bf3 Ne6 31. Kg3
{It seems that Black loses the pawn on a7 now, but he seems to have sufficient
activity to compensate for it} Rd3 32. Rd5 {White can't afford to grab the
pawn yet} (32. Rxa7 Nd4 33. Ra3 Ne2+ 34. Kh2 Rxa3 35. Rxa3 Nxf4 {And it is not
clear who is better anymore}) 32... Rxd5 $2 {But this is a mistake, after
which White gets back in the driver's seat} (32... Rbd1 {Is a move negine will
quickly point out. After} 33. Rxd3 Rxd3 34. Rxa7 Rd4 35. a4 Nxf4 {Black has
every chance of defending}) 33. Bxd5 {Now bishops gets in a good position and
dominates the knight} Nc7 34. Bb3 a6 35. Rc4 Nb5 36. Rc8+ Ke7 37. Ra8 $6 {
There was actually an immediate win available} (37. Bd5 {Is pointed out by the
engine. After} Rd1 38. Bc6 {White is winning}) 37... Nc7 38. Rc8 Rc1 39. Kf2
Rc5 40. Ke2 Rc6 41. Kd3 Rc5 $6 {Too passive.} (41... f6 {For better or for
worse, Black should have tried eliminating the pawns, although his position
remains difficult}) 42. g3 Rc6 43. Bc4 Rc5 (43... f6) 44. a4 Rc6 45. Kd4 a5 46.
Kd3 Rc5 47. Rb8 f6 {But now this comes at a wrong moment} 48. exf6+ Kxf6 49.
Rb6+ {And Black will lose at least an exchange, so Zelcic resigned. The
continuation could have been} Kg7 50. Kd4 Rxc4+ 51. Kxc4 {And wins} 1-0

