1. d4 d6 2. Nf3 g6 {Jovanovic plays the Modern, the Philidor and similar
systems his whole life} 3. e4 {But this surprises me - Sasa enters the Pirc.
Not something very common for a d4 player} Nf6 4. Nc3 c6 5. Be3 Qa5 6. Bd3 Bg7
7. Qd2 Bg4 {I am not sure about the combination of the moves c6-Qa5-Bg4, but I
don't believe it can lead to something good} 8. Nh4 $1 {But this is a strong
and far from obvious reply. The knight simply moves away from the attack and
makes way for the Facundo the f-pawn.} e5 {Logical continuation} 9. h3 Be6 10.
f4 Nh5 $2 {But this is too provocative. Black asks for trouble} (10... exd4 {
The crisis in the center should have been resolved. After} 11. Bxd4 c5 12. Be3
Nc6 13. f5 Bd7 {White is better, but Black is in the game} 14. g4 {Is not
nearly as dangerous as in the game}) 11. dxe5 dxe5 12. f5 {Now this is very
strong} Bf6 {From frying pan to fire} (12... Bd7 {Now leads to} 13. g4) 13. O-O
{Not strictly neccessary, but very attractive and strong pawn sacrifice} Bxh4
14. fxe6 fxe6 15. Rad1 {Black can't castle, his pieces are on the edge or not
developed and he is in serious trouble} Qb4 $2 {The final mistake, allowing
coup de grace} (15... Nd7 {Leads to} 16. Bc4 O-O-O 17. Bxe6) (15... Qd8 {Is
relatively best, but after} 16. g4 Ng7 (16... Ng3 17. Rf3) 17. Na4 {White's
compensation is enormous}) 16. Nb5 {Almost like Morphy} Qxd2 17. Nd6+ Kd8 18.
Rxd2 {Despite the queen exchange, Black is busted} Nd7 19. Rf7 $1 (19. Nf7+ Ke7
20. Nxh8 Rxh8 {Was, of course, sufficient, but Sasa goes for the kill}) 19...
Kc7 20. Bc4 Nhf6 21. Bxe6 {Black is completely paralyzed. The game ends quickly
} Rad8 22. g3 {A final touch in a position where every combination is "as
natural as baby's smile"} Bxg3 23. Bg5 Rdf8 24. Bxf6 Rxf7 25. Nxf7 Nxf6 26.
Nxh8 {And here Jovanovic resigned. A real gem that well deserved the award it
got!} 1-0

