{This endgame is a dead-draw. Kurajica apparently relaxed and though he can
draw as he wants. But it was not meant to be} 60. Rb1 {A tricky move, setting
the final trap} Kd6 $4 {Falling right into it. Almost anything else drew} (
60... Kf7 61. Rg1 Kg6 {And White can't take on g4} 62. Rxg4 (62. Rg2 Kh5 63.
Kf3 h3 64. Rxg4 fxg4+ 65. Kg3 Kg6 {And it is a dead draw}) 62... fxg4) (60...
Rg3 {Was also sufficient. After} 61. Rh1 Rg4 62. Rg1 Kf7 {We get to the same
thing as in previous variation}) 61. Rg1 $1 {Oh horrors! Black's king is way
too far. White can force Black to exchange rooks, after which he will have an
easy king and pawn ending} Ke7 62. Rg2 Kf7 63. Kf3 {And now it is all over -
the Black king is too far away} h3 64. Rh2 Rh4 65. Kg3 Rg4+ 66. Kxh3 Rg1 67.
Re2 Rh1+ 68. Kg2 Rb1 69. Rc2 Rb6 70. Rc7+ Kg6 71. Re7 Ra6 72. Kf3 Rb6 73. Ke2
Ra6 74. Kd2 Ra2+ 75. Kc1 Ra6 76. Kb2 Rb6+ 77. Ka3 Kh5 78. Ka4 Kg6 79. Ka5 Rc6
80. Kb5 Rd6 81. Ra7 Rd8 82. Kc6 Rc8+ 83. Kd6 {I can only imagine how Kurajica
felt after this.} 1-0

