{Saric was significantly better earlier in the game, but failed to find the
best defence. Here Brkic is close to equalizing.} 40... Bc3 $2 {But this move
loses immediately} (40... Bg7 $1 {Was the only move. It is much more resilient.
After} 41. Rxe4 (41. Re8+ {Might be a better try} Kh7 42. Re7 Kg8 43. Bc5 a3 {
But it is not clear if White is winning here}) 41... a3 42. Ra4 Rb2 {The
bishop on b6 is hanging. White probably has to bail out by giving it up,
because after} 43. Bd4 Bxd4 44. exd4 a2 {He is the one losing the game}) (40...
Bb2 {Also prevents Rb2} 41. Rxe4 a3 42. Ra4) (40... Ba1 {Also leaves the
bishop prone to attacks:} 41. Rxe4 a3 42. Ra4 Rb2 43. Rxa3 Rxb6 44. Rxa1) 41.
Rxe4 a3 42. Ra4 {The point! Now the bishop on c3 will be under attack of the
rook on a4 and the game is lost} Be5 43. Bc5 Kf7 44. Rxa3 Rc2 45. Bd4 Bxg3 46.
h5 Ke6 47. h6 Rh2 48. Bg7 Rh4 49. Kg2 Bc7 50. Ra7 Bd6 51. Ra6 Kd7 52. Kf3 Be7
53. Kg3 Rh1 54. Kg4 Ke8 55. Be5 Kf7 56. Bf4 Bf6 57. Kf5 Rh5+ 58. Ke4 Rh4 59.
Ra2 Bg5 60. Ra7+ Kf6 61. h7 Kg6 62. h8=Q Rxh8 63. Ra6+ {It is simply amazing
how much value a single move has in the engame} 1-0

