1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. Nc3 a6 4. Be2 Nc6 5. d4 cxd4 6. Nxd4 Qc7 7. O-O Nf6 8.
Be3 Be7 9. f4 d6 10. Kh1 O-O 11. Qe1 Nxd4 12. Bxd4 b5 13. Qg3 Bb7 14. a3 Rad8
15. Rae1 Rd7 16. Bd3 Qd8 17. Qh3 g6 18. f5 e5 19. Be3 Re8 20. fxg6 hxg6 {White
has played a very nice against the Sicilian and has a very nice edge. Most of
us would play something positional here, but Wei goes for the immediate kill}
21. Nd5 $1 Nxd5 {[pgndiagram]} 22. Rxf7 $3 {As they say, a bolt from the blue}
Kxf7 {The best testament of the depth of the combination is the fact that even
computer takes some time to conclude that Black is completely busted here} 23.
Qh7+ Ke6 24. exd5+ Kxd5 {[pgndiagram]} (24... Bxd5 25. Bxg6 {And Black is
busted} Bxg2+ 26. Kxg2 d5 27. Bf7+ Kd6 28. Qh6+ Bf6 29. Bxe8) 25. Be4+ $3 Kxe4
26. Qf7 $3 {An amazing quiet move, cutting the king's retreat and threatening
mate} Bf6 27. Bd2+ Kd4 (27... Kf5 28. Rf1+ {Is mate in a couple of moves} Ke4
29. Qb3) 28. Be3+ Ke4 {[pgndiagram]} 29. Qb3 $3 Kf5 30. Rf1+ Kg4 {[pgndiagram]}
31. Qd3 $3 {Once again the only move that wins} Bxg2+ (31... Rg8 32. Qe2+ Kh4
33. Rf3 Bxf3 34. Qxf3 {And there is no defence against Qh3 mate}) 32. Kxg2 Qa8+
33. Kg1 Bg5 34. Qe2+ Kh4 35. Bf2+ Kh3 36. Be1 {With Rf3 and Qg2 coming, Black
decided he has had enough.. Although it might have been more sporting to play
it out till the end and acknowledge the brilliancy of the young chinese.} 1-0
